      "path": "SKILL.md",
      "content": "---\n\n## name: character-identity-card description: Create a production-ready multi-view character identity card from one or more reference images plus optional art direction. Use for character identity locking, face-angle references, body turnarounds, rear-hairstyle references, and consistent AI image or video production. Clearly separate observed traits from requested or inferred details.\n\n# Character Identity Card\n\nTurn one or more character reference images plus optional art direction into a reusable, production-ready multi-view identity card for consistent AI image and video generation. Identity specifications and model-ready prompts support the card-generation workflow; they are not the primary product.\n\n## Required inputs\n\n- At least one usable character reference image.\n- The user's custom direction: wardrobe, age/presentation, realism, intended platform, and any must-keep or must-change traits.\n\nMultiple angles improve reliability but are not mandatory. Separate what is **observed**, **requested**, and **inferred**. Never present inferred anatomy, body proportions, or hidden details as facts from the source image.\n\nBefore generating or editing, inspect every local image with the available image-viewing tool. Label each input image's role: identity anchor, body/wardrobe reference, style reference, or layout reference.\n\n## Choose the deliverable\n\n1. **Identity card (default)** — a generated multi-panel card plus the observed/requested/inferred specification and validation notes.\n2. **Identity specification only** — a reusable identity lock without generating an image; include prompts only when requested or operationally useful.\n3. **Platform adaptation** — adapt the locked identity and card instructions for a named image/video platform.\n\nIf the user supplies references and direction without naming a deliverable, default to an identity card. For a card, use the image-generation capability and read references/card-spec.md before generation. Read references/prompt-template.md when drafting the generation prompt or an optional platform prompt.\n\n## Core workflow\n\n1. Extract only visually supported identity anchors: facial geometry, hair silhouette, complexion range, apparent age range, body silhouette, wardrobe, and distinctive asymmetries.\n2. Resolve contradictions across references by prioritizing, in order: the user's explicit instruction, the designated identity anchor, repeated evidence across images, then cautious inference.\n3. Produce an identity lock that describes relationships and proportions, not vague beauty adjectives.\n4. Select a body-panel mode:\n   - `headless-body` for reliable distant-body assets. The front and side/three-quarter body panels are cleanly framed from the collar/shoulder line to the shoes, with white negative space above. The 180-degree back body panel is the required exception: show the complete rear figure from the back of the head to the shoes so the rear hairstyle and head silhouette remain visible. It must face directly away and reveal no facial features or side-face profile. Do not blur, mosaic, pixelate, erase, or show an anatomical neck stump.\n   - `full-head` when the user explicitly needs conventional full-body turnarounds and accepts the higher risk of face drift.\n5. Generate the card from the references, preserving identity and wardrobe. The reference image is evidence, not an edit target, unless the user explicitly requests an edit.\n6. Inspect the result for identity drift, panel completeness, limb errors, garment inconsistency, accidental face content in the headless front/side panels, and a missing, cropped, or face-revealing head in the back panel. Make at most two focused revisions unless the user asks to continue.\n7. Return the final image and the observed/requested/inferred identity specification. Also return the exact generation prompt for reproducibility; add a compact platform prompt when requested or useful for a point-consuming tool.\n\n## Non-negotiable invariants\n\n- Every clear face panel must depict the same person: consistent skull shape, eye spacing, nose structure, lip shape, jawline, ears, hairline, hair color, and apparent age.\n- Body panels must keep the same height impression, shoulder width, torso-to-leg ratio, garment construction, colors, accessories, and footwear.\n- In `headless-body` mode, the back panel must preserve the complete rear head and hairstyle. If the reference does not show the rear hairstyle, derive the most conservative continuation of the visible hair silhouette and label it as inferred rather than observed.\n- Use a neutral white studio background, soft standardized lighting, and panel separators. Do not introduce scenery, props, logos, captions, watermarks, or decorative typography unless requested.\n- Preserve natural skin microtexture without beauty-filter smoothing, plastic skin, fake pore noise, aggressive sharpening, or exaggerated HDR.\n- A reference-based result is an approximation. Do not claim the original generator prompt, seed, LoRA, model, or hidden settings were recovered.\n- For an identifiable real person's likeness, confirm the user has permission for the intended reuse when that is not already clear. Do not frame an unauthorized likeness replica as a reusable commercial identity.\n\n## Output structure\n\nKeep the analysis concise and production-oriented:\n\n```text\nMode: identity card | identity specification | platform adaptation\nBody-panel mode: headless-body | full-head\nObserved identity anchors: ...\nRequested direction: ...\nInferred or unresolved details: ...\nIdentity lock: ...\nExact generation prompt: ... (for identity-card output)\nCompact platform prompt: ... (optional)\nValidation notes: ...\n```\n\nWhen an image is generated, save the final selected asset into the current workspace and report its absolute path.",
      "contentType": "text/markdown",
      "primary": true
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Character Identity Card\n\nAn Agent Skill for creating a production-ready multi-view character identity card from one or more reference images plus optional art direction.\n\n中文：这是一个用于 AI 图片与短视频角色资产生产的角色身份卡 Skill。输入一张或多张参考图以及可选的服装、年龄、身高或风格要求，即可生成稳定的多视角角色身份卡。身份描述和提示词用于支持身份卡生产，不是主要产品。\n\n## What it does\n\n- Extracts visually supported face, hair, body, and wardrobe directions.\n- Separates **observed**, **requested**, and **inferred** information.\n- Produces a geometry-based identity lock instead of vague beauty adjectives.\n- Defaults to generating an identity card when the user provides references without naming a deliverable.\n- Also supports identity-specification-only and platform-adaptation deliverables.\n- Provides `headless-body` and `full-head` body-panel modes.\n- Validates identity consistency, garment continuity, anatomy, skin texture, and panel completeness.\n- Keeps the complete rear head and hairstyle visible in the back body panel while avoiding distant-face drift in front and side body panels.\n\n## Safety and scope\n\n- This Skill does not recover an original hidden prompt, seed, model, LoRA, or private generation settings.\n- Reference-based results are approximations.\n- Do not use identifiable real-person likenesses without permission for the intended reuse.\n- When permission is unavailable, use references only for broad, non-identifying directions and create a new fictional identity.\n- Do not publish user reference images or generated likeness assets without the necessary rights.\n\n## Repository structure\n\n```text\ncharacter-identity-card/\n├── SKILL.md\n├── agents/\n│   └── openai.yaml\n└── references/\n    ├── card-spec.md\n    └── prompt-template.md\n```\n\n## Installation\n\n### Codex\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/cadyyue-blip/character-identity-card.git \\\n  ~/.codex/skills/character-identity-card\n```\n\nRestart the agent session if the new Skill is not discovered immediately.\n\n### Other Agent Skills-compatible tools\n\nClone or copy this repository into the tool's Skill directory. The entry point is `SKILL.md`; supporting rules are under `references/`.\n\n## Usage\n\nInvoke the Skill and provide at least one usable character reference plus the intended direction:\n\n```text\nUse $character-identity-card.\nCreate an identity card from these references.\nWardrobe: minimal basics.\nPresentation: photorealistic young adult.\nBody-panel mode: headless-body.\nMust keep: the rear hairstyle visible in the back body panel.\n```\n\nThe Skill can return:\n\n```text\nMode: identity card | identity specification | platform adaptation\nBody-panel mode: headless-body | full-head\nObserved identity anchors: ...\nRequested direction: ...\nInferred or unresolved details: ...\nIdentity lock: ...\nExact generation prompt: ...\nCompact platform prompt: ... (optional)\nValidation notes: ...\n```\n\nImage generation is performed by the image-generation capability available in the host agent. This repository does not bundle a model, API key, or image-generation backend.\n\n## Using it with LibTV / LiblibAI\n\nThis repository is a **character identity-card creation Skill**. LibTV's official `libtv-skill` is a separate execution Skill that connects an agent to LibTV for image and video generation.\n\nRecommended composition:\n\n1. Install this Skill to create the character identity card, identity lock, generation prompt, and validation rules.\n2. Install the official `libtv-labs/libtv-skills` integration and configure its required LibTV access credentials according to its documentation.\n3. Ask the agent to use this Skill first, then pass the finalized generation prompt and permitted reference assets to `libtv-skill` for execution.\n4. Keep the generated identity card as the identity anchor for later LibTV image-to-video or multi-shot workflows.\n\nPublishing this repository on GitHub does not automatically list it inside LibTV. To request inclusion in LibTV's official repository, open an Issue or submit a Pull Request to `libtv-labs/libtv-skills` and follow the maintainers' review requirements.\n\n## License\n\nMIT. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).",
      "contentType": "text/markdown",
      "primary": false
    },
    {
      "path": "references/card-spec.md",
      "content": "# Character identity card specification\n\nUse this reference only when generating a multi-panel character card.\n\n## Default portrait layout\n\nUse a clean 3:4 portrait canvas with thin white or very light-gray gutters.\n\n- **Upper-left, large panel (about 42% width):** clear frontal head-and-shoulders identity anchor, neutral expression, direct gaze.\n- **Upper-right, three narrow panels:** front body, side or three-quarter body, and back body.\n- **Bottom row, four equal panels:** left profile, left three-quarter, frontal head-and-shoulders, and right three-quarter.\n\nAll panels use the same wardrobe, grooming, apparent age, skin tone, and studio-lighting logic. Default to no labels because generated typography introduces noise; add labels only when requested.\n\n## Headless distant-body mode\n\nThis is the recommended mode when the sheet will feed distant AI-video shots.\n\n- The front and side/three-quarter body views show the complete garment and body from the collar/shoulder line to the shoes.\n- In those two views, the frame or editorial mask ends cleanly at the collar line; white negative space occupies the area where a head would otherwise appear.\n- The back body view is the required exception: show the complete rear figure from the crown/back of the head to the shoes. Preserve the back-of-head shape, rear hair volume, direction, length, taper, and nape silhouette consistent with the identity anchor.\n- The back body view must be a true 180-degree rear view. No eyes, nose, mouth, cheek, or readable side-face profile may be visible; ears may appear only as naturally limited by the hairstyle and exact rear angle.\n- Never crop, erase, mask, or leave blank the head in the back body view.\n- Never use face blur, mosaic, pixelation, smearing, an empty oval, or a visibly severed neck.\n- Do not try to preserve facial identity in the small front or side/three-quarter body panels. The separate high-resolution face panels are the only face source for downstream composition.\n- If no reference shows the rear hairstyle, use the most conservative anatomical continuation of the visible hair silhouette and report it as inferred. Do not invent a different cut, length, part, accessory, or decorative styling.\n\n## Full-head mode\n\nUse only when requested. Keep the face visible in all body panels, but treat the large face anchor and bottom-row face views as the authoritative identity references. Reject an output if distant faces visibly become a different person.\n\n## Studio and capture standard\n\n- Pure neutral-white seamless background, uniform and texture-free.\n- Soft global studio light, neutral approximately 5000–5300 K; a large diffused key slightly off-axis and restrained fill.\n- Soft rectangular catchlights in clear face panels.\n- Minimal cast shadow and no dramatic rim light.\n- Natural perspective: portrait-style focal length for face panels and low-distortion catalog perspective for body panels.\n- Neutral stance, relaxed shoulders, arms naturally lowered, hands and feet anatomically correct.\n\n## Identity validation checklist\n\nReject or revise when any of these occur:\n\n- eye spacing, eyelid shape, nose bridge/tip, lip contour, jaw width, ear placement, hairline, or apparent age changes between face panels;\n- garment lapels, buttons, tie, skirt/trouser cut, hem length, socks, shoes, or accessories change between body views;\n- body height impression or torso-to-leg ratio changes;\n- front or side/three-quarter body panels contain head or face pixels in `headless-body` mode;\n- the back body panel in `headless-body` mode omits or crops the head, fails to show the rear hairstyle, turns away from a true rear view, or reveals facial features/side profile;\n- skin is waxy, over-smoothed, over-sharpened, or covered by synthetic pore noise;\n- extra fingers, fused limbs, duplicated accessories, text, logos, props, or background scenery appear.\n\nDo not reject harmless changes in perspective, natural lighting falloff, or tiny strand-level hair variation.",
      "contentType": "text/markdown",
      "primary": false
    },
    {
      "path": "references/prompt-template.md",
      "content": "# Prompt templates\n\nUse only the clauses supported by the references and the user's direction. Replace bracketed fields; do not leave placeholders in the delivered prompt.\n\n## Production identity-card prompt\n\n```text\nCreate one standardized multi-panel character identity card of exactly the same [character description] based on the supplied identity-reference images. Preserve the character's observable facial structure: [identity anchors]. Preserve [hair], [complexion], [body silhouette], and [wardrobe]. Do not beautify, idealize, or redesign the person.\n\nLayout: a clean 3:4 portrait contact sheet. Upper left is one large, sharply resolved frontal head-and-shoulders portrait with a neutral expression and direct gaze. Upper right contains three narrow body-turnaround panels in this order: front, side/three-quarter, back. Bottom row contains four equal head-and-shoulders views: left profile, left three-quarter, front, right three-quarter. Every clear face panel must be recognizably the same person, with identical apparent age, skull shape, eye spacing and eyelid form, nose bridge and tip, lip contour, jawline, ears, hairline, and hair color.\n\n[BODY MODE CLAUSE]\n\nThe background is a pure neutral-white seamless studio, clean and uniform, with thin light gutters separating panels; no environment, furniture, props, logos, labels, captions, or watermarks. Use standardized professional studio photography: a large diffused key light slightly off-axis, restrained fill, neutral 5000–5300 K color, soft rectangular catchlights, natural tonal separation, minimal cast shadow, and no dramatic grading.\n\nRender realistic human skin rather than cosmetic perfection: visible but subtle pores with physical depth, natural eyelid folds and under-eye texture, fine peach fuzz under side light, restrained micro-shadowing, slight regional color variation, and natural low-level skin sheen. Keep facial bone structure and skin relief. Use fine organic film grain and optical clarity without digital edge sharpening.\n\nAvoid beauty-filter skin, plastic or wax skin, fake pore noise, excessive makeup, influencer-face homogenization, face drift, age drift, body-proportion drift, garment changes, asymmetrical panel scale, extra fingers, fused limbs, malformed hands or feet, duplicated accessories, CG/game-render appearance, painterly texture, over-HDR, oversharpening, smearing, facial blur, mosaic, or pixelation.\n```\n\nUse one of these body-mode clauses:\n\n### Headless body clause\n\n```text\nFor the front and side/three-quarter body panels only, use a clean editorial crop/mask at the collar and shoulder line so each body asset runs from shoulders to shoes with white negative space above. No face or head pixels appear in these two panels. For the back body panel, do not apply the headless crop: show one true 180-degree rear view of the complete person from the crown/back of the head to the shoes. Clearly preserve the back-of-head silhouette and rear hairstyle—hair volume, direction, length, taper, and nape shape—consistent with the identity reference. The rear head faces directly away from camera; show no eyes, nose, mouth, cheek, or readable side-face profile. Do not crop, erase, blank, blur, mosaic, pixelate, or smear the rear head, and do not create a severed-neck effect. The separate close-up face panels remain the sole facial-identity source.\n```\n\n### Full-head body clause\n\n```text\nFor all three body panels, show the complete person from head to shoes. Distant faces remain the same identity as the large frontal portrait, without simplification, distortion, blur, or substitution.\n```\n\n## Compact prompt for point-consuming tools\n\n```text\n同一角色身份卡，严格参考输入人物。3:4白底摄影棚拼版：左上大幅正脸半身；右上正面、侧面、背面身体；下排左侧脸、左45°、正脸、右45°。锁定脸型、眼距眼形、鼻唇、下颌、耳朵、发际线、发型、年龄、肤色、身材比例和服装。自然真实皮肤纹理，柔和中性棚拍光，禁止美颜、塑料皮、变脸、变年龄、服装漂移、肢体错误、文字水印。[精简身体模式要求]\n```\n\nFor headless mode, replace the final placeholder with:\n\n```text\n正面与侧面/侧前方身体视图从衣领肩线到鞋完整展示，头部区域干净留白；背面必须为严格180°完整后视，从后脑勺发顶到鞋全部入镜，保留与参考一致的后脑勺轮廓、发量走向、长度、收尾和后颈发际线。背面不露眼鼻口、脸颊或可辨识侧脸；不得裁掉、抹除、留白、模糊或马赛克处理后脑勺，不出现断颈。\n```\n\nFor full-head mode, replace it with:\n\n```text\n身体三视图完整显示头到脚，远景脸仍须与主正脸完全同一身份。\n```\n\n## Identity lock syntax\n\nDescribe observable geometry and relationships instead of aesthetic rankings. Prefer:\n\n```text\n[apparent age range]; [face length-to-width impression]; [jaw/chin geometry]; [eye spacing and eyelid form]; [brow direction]; [nose bridge/tip/alar relationship]; [lip contour and volume]; [ear placement]; [hairline and hair silhouette]; [stable asymmetries or marks].\n```\n\nAvoid unsupported ethnicity, personality, class, health, or attractiveness claims. If a requested body or rear view is not visible in any source, state that it is designed from the user's instruction rather than recovered from the reference.",
      "contentType": "text/markdown",
      "primary": false
    }
  ],
